    {
      "id": "claim_17a28afbddb744c3bdb0777d5378da84",
      "statement": "run-code --raw result decoding is version-sensitive: Playwright CLI 0.1.19 encodes a returned JSON string once more as a JSON string literal, so the runtime performs a double-decode (JSON.parse then, if the value is a string, JSON.parse again) before validating the envelope; changing the version pin without re-validating this behavior is unsafe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://skills/website-automation-builder/assets/site-template/src/runtime/cli-browser.ts#L204-L211",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fceb96e4383192abf9e7fa66509dc14755fbc4072b8dba401623881de74dd8d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://skills/website-automation-builder/references/sources.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8fd9844544ebce65b199ce97c2be4d101c9c0e9a7e67008242a73a2d706d53d2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_034441be292443eab1baa85944e6026c",
      "statement": "The runtime executes precompiled per-action bundles inside the CLI's browser VM by serializing the verified actions/<id>.js bundle (SHA-256 + size checked) into an async page wrapper written as an exclusive file under .local/run-code/<uuid>.js and invoking -s=<session> --raw run-code --filename=<path>; the wrapper is serialization only and the prebuilt function owns all behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://skills/website-automation-builder/assets/site-template/src/runtime/cli-browser.ts#L170-L242",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01404d706c5734d730a228132ea9fd470e5d6e4f4cf9e9a41ba0c917de56c490:"
        },
        {
