    {
      "id": "claim_3bbcc444a3a7481a9de18368edb22735",
      "statement": "The browser VM that executes run-code lacks the usual Node globals (URL, TextEncoder, Buffer, process), so the precompiled code uses ECMAScript-only origin and UTF-8 size checks (string-based origin validation, not the WHATWG URL global) instead of Node APIs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://skills/website-automation-builder/references/sources.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8fd9844544ebce65b199ce97c2be4d101c9c0e9a7e67008242a73a2d706d53d2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a98bb19145a3409a83eaa48fce07a211",
      "statement": "The runtime shells out to the CLI via execFile (never a shell string), binding each purpose to a bounded timeout and buffer: list/attach use a 30 s timeout while runtime (run-code) is bounded by config.actionBudgetMs; maxBuffer is always config.maxCliBytes, and subprocess failures are classified into BROWSER_REQUIRED / ATTACH_FAILED / CLI_PROTOCOL by purpose and message content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://artifacts/demo-automation/site.config.ts#L11-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33a1fb33fd5b0e8a8085acddbae1848a9416d02f2b5fd523a5777fd29dd4c840:"
