    {
      "id": "claim_962f4ba748b348469afb8e32d3131219",
      "statement": "For portable deployments (scripts/site-runtime.mjs), the CliBrowser constructor accepts a browser.cliScript override: the bundled CLI JS entry point is invoked through process.execPath instead of playwright-cli on PATH (on Windows this avoids shell .cmd wrappers); the protocol is unchanged and there is no agent-provided executable override.",
      "evidence": [
        {
